  "articleBody": "It's a common frustration: your website looks great, has tons of info, but when someone asks an AI assistant about your services, your business doesn't pop up. What gives? Well, AI systems don't \"read\" websites the same way humans do. They're looking for very specific signals, and if your site isn't set up to provide them, you could be missing out. Things like outdated FAQs, heavy website themes that slow down AI crawlers, or a lack of structured data (that's the fancy way of saying clear, machine-readable information) can all make your business a ghost to Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and other answer engines.\n\nFirst, think about your content. Is it directly answering common questions people ask about your services, or is it more brochure-like? AI loves clear, concise answers. Next, consider your site's technical foundation. Many popular website builders use a lot of code that, while making your site pretty for people, can make it clunky for AI to crawl and understand quickly. Finally, if you're not using JSON-LD schema — a specific way to tag your content so AI knows what it's looking at — you're leaving a lot on the table. This structured data helps AI understand everything from your business name and address to your specific services, making it much easier for them to recommend you when relevant questions come up.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process\nWhen you start working on AI visibility, expect a deep dive into your existing content and technical setup. It's not just about adding a few keywords; it's about re-architecting how your information is presented to machines. This often involves researching the exact questions your ideal clients are asking on platforms like Quora or Reddit, then generating new, fact-dense content that directly answers those questions. You'll also see a focus on converting your content into clean, static HTML with rich schema, making it super easy for AI to digest. Finally, this optimized content gets published to dedicated \"AI Resource Libraries\" on platforms like GitHub, which are known for being trusted by AI systems. It's a comprehensive approach that ensures your expertise is truly machine-readable.\n\nReady to get seen by AI? Let's chat about how we can make your business an AI answer engine favorite.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
